# MVP 1 — Milestone-Based Implementation Plan

Purpose: give this to an AI coding assistant (Claude Code, Copilot, Cursor, etc.) **one milestone at a time**, not all at once. Each milestone is small, testable on its own, and builds on the previous one.

Stack: ASP.NET Core Web API, Blazor WebAssembly, EF Core, Postgres/SQL Server, OpenRouter (GLM-5.2 for MVP1).

---

## Milestone 0 — Project Skeleton (no AI yet)

**Goal:** Basic solution structure runs locally, nothing smart yet.

**Scope:**

- ASP.NET Core Web API project (`SpecPlatform.Api`)
- Blazor WebAssembly project (`SpecPlatform.Client`)
- Shared class library for DTOs (`SpecPlatform.Shared`)
- EF Core + Postgres/SQL Server connection configured
- One health-check endpoint (`GET /api/health`) returning `200 OK`
- Blazor app can call the health-check endpoint and display "API is alive"

**Test it yourself:**

- Run API + Blazor app locally, see "API is alive" on screen
- No auth, no AI, no real data yet — just confirming the skeleton wires together

---

## Milestone 1 — Project + Spec Data Model + CRUD (no AI yet)

**Goal:** Can create a project/team container, then create/read/update specs under it (no brainstorming UI yet).

**Scope:**

- EF Core entities:
  - `Project` (Id, Name, Description, CreatedAt) — the parent container for a team/product/feature area
  - `Spec` (Id, ProjectId, Title, Description, Status, CreatedAt) — now belongs to a Project
  - `SpecVersion` (SpecId, VersionNumber, Content, PublishedAt)
  - `AcceptanceCriterion` (SpecVersionId, Text)
  - `ScopeTag` (SpecVersionId, TagName e.g. "bff"/"api"/"mfe")
- API endpoints:
  - `POST /api/projects` (create a project), `GET /api/projects`, `GET /api/projects/{id}`
  - `POST /api/projects/{projectId}/specs` (create a draft spec under a project), `GET /api/specs/{id}`, `PUT /api/specs/{id}` (edit draft), `POST /api/specs/{id}/publish` (creates a new version)
- Simple Blazor UI:
  - Project list/creation screen (name a project, e.g. "Loan Approval Feature" or "PrivateLendingCommon MFE")
  - Selecting a project shows its specs (empty at first)
  - "New Spec" only available _within_ a selected project — no orphan specs
  - Create a spec, add acceptance criteria, add scope tags, save as draft, publish

**Test it yourself:**

- Create a project, confirm it appears in the list
- Create a spec under that project, publish it, confirm version 1 exists and is correctly linked to the project
- Create a second project, confirm its spec list is separate/isolated from the first project's specs
- Edit and publish again, confirm version 2 is created and version 1 is preserved (not overwritten)

