## Milestone 4 — Notifications on Publish

**Goal:** When a spec is published, relevant people get notified (simple version — no subscriptions system yet).

**Scope:**

- On publish, send a simple notification: email (or just a webhook/console log for MVP) saying "{SpecTitle} updated to v{N}"
- Hardcode the notification target for now (e.g. one email address or one webhook URL) — no per-user subscription management yet, that's a v2 feature
- Notification includes a short AI-generated summary of what changed (reuse the diff logic from Milestone 3, feed it to GLM-5.2 to phrase it in plain English: "2 acceptance criteria changed in the auth section")

**Test it yourself:**

- Publish a new version, confirm the notification fires and the summary text is accurate and readable

---

## Milestone 5 — Basic Auth (Entra ID, single tenant to start)

**Goal:** Only logged-in users can access the app — proves the SSO integration works before going multi-tenant.

**Scope:**

- Register the app in your own Entra ID tenant
- Add Microsoft.Identity.Web to the API, MSAL-based auth to the Blazor WASM client
- Require login to access any spec endpoint
- No multi-tenant support yet, no per-company permissions — just "can I log in with my Microsoft 365 account at all"

**Test it yourself:**

- Confirm you can log in with your own Microsoft 365 account and reach the spec dashboard
- Confirm an unauthenticated request to the API is rejected

---

## What's intentionally NOT in these milestones (comes after MVP1 is proven)

- Multi-tenant SSO (any company's Entra ID)
- Commenting/feedback loop
- Jira integration
- Team/role permissions
- Blob storage / attachments
- Polished CLI packaging (global tool, installer)

---

## How to use this with an AI assistant

Give the assistant **one milestone section at a time**, in order. After each milestone, test it yourself against the "Test it yourself" checklist before moving to the next prompt. Don't paste the whole document as one instruction — that defeats the purpose of incremental, testable delivery.
